name 'iterating-with-ai-preassessment-q7_2025'

question 'Why should a developer include labels (like "Price:" or "Category:") when rendering a complex object record?'

wrong 'To make the code easier for the AI to read.'
right 'To reduce the chance of the user misinterpreting raw data values.'
wrong 'Because JavaScript objects cannot be displayed without labels.'
wrong 'To make the list of items sort faster.'

allow_multiple_attempts true

teacher_markdown <<MARKDOWN
Lesson 5

Raw data (like `true` or `45`) can be confusing. Labels provide context, ensuring the user understands what the information represents, which improves inclusivity and clarity.
MARKDOWN
